privacy='''<p class="legal-date">Updated and effective October 5, 2026</p><div class="callout"><p><strong>FeedFare turns steps into screen time.</strong> This policy covers native FeedFare, older installed subscription versions, TestFlight builds, and this website. Practices can differ by the version you use.</p></div>
<h2>1. Who is responsible</h2><p>FeedFare is developed by Nick Rae in Merced, California. For questions or privacy requests, email <a href="mailto:nick@nickrae.net">nick@nickrae.net</a>. You do not need to create a FeedFare account to use the app.</p>
<h2>2. Steps, progress, and app protection</h2><p>With your permission, FeedFare reads step counts from Apple Health and uses your device’s Motion &amp; Fitness data for step counting. This supports walking goals, earned screen time, history, and streaks. Apple Watch steps may be included after they sync to Apple Health. FeedFare does not write or change your Health records.</p><p>Your goals, preferences, progress, earned balance, and sessions are stored in the app’s local storage. In the native version, Screen Time provides opaque selection tokens for the apps you choose. The app and its protection extensions share selection and session state in an on-device App Group. The native app does not send those tokens or step history to a FeedFare server.</p><p>The native version may import existing FeedFare progress and keep a local migration backup. Device or iCloud backups are governed by your Apple backup settings; on-device storage does not mean that the operating system can never back it up.</p>
<h2>3. Permissions and optional features</h2><ul><li><strong>Health:</strong> reading steps for progress and earned time.</li><li><strong>Motion &amp; Fitness:</strong> live step counting on the device.</li><li><strong>Screen Time:</strong> selecting and protecting apps and managing timed access.</li><li><strong>Notifications:</strong> optional reminders that you can turn off.</li><li><strong>Sharing:</strong> when you choose to share a milestone, the information in that image goes to the app or recipient you select.</li></ul><p>FeedFare does not need contacts or location to provide its walking features. You can revoke permissions in iOS settings. Features that need a revoked permission may stop working. See <a href="https://feedfare.app/support.html#permissions">permission help</a>.</p>
<h2>4. Purchases: native app and older subscription versions</h2><p>Apple processes App Store purchases and subscriptions. FeedFare does not receive your payment-card details. Older installed subscription versions use RevenueCat to validate purchases and determine access. This can involve purchase history, transaction or receipt information, subscription status, and a pseudonymous app user identifier. RevenueCat does not receive your step counts through FeedFare’s purchase integration.</p><p>Native FeedFare 2026.9.28 does not include the RevenueCat SDK, advertising SDKs, or a third-party analytics SDK. Its full app access does not require a subscription. Apple still handles app acquisition and any previous subscription records. FeedFare’s previous subscription plans have been retired and no longer renew; this is separate from installing an app update. People who continue using older versions may still use those versions’ purchase services.</p><p>See <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy">RevenueCat’s privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple’s privacy policy</a> for their services.</p>
<h2>5. Website, diagnostics, and support</h2><p>This website is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub and its delivery providers process technical request information, such as IP address, browser details, and request logs, to serve and protect the site. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>. Fonts, styles, and images used by the page are served with the site. We do not add advertising pixels, analytics cookies, or a third-party website tracking SDK.</p><p>App Store links may include a campaign label identifying where the link was placed. Apple can provide campaign-level acquisition reports subject to its reporting rules. Those labels do not include your Health data, Screen Time selections, or a personal identifier generated by this website.</p><p>Apple may provide app diagnostics or TestFlight feedback according to your Apple sharing settings and any feedback you choose to send. If you contact support, we receive your email address and the information you include. Send only what is needed to explain the issue; private Health records are not required.</p>
<h2>6. Sharing and use</h2><p>We use information to provide the features you choose, handle purchase access in subscription versions, respond to support requests, and maintain the app and website. We do not sell personal information or use step data or Screen Time selections for advertising. Service providers process the information needed for their roles described above. Information may also be disclosed when required by law or to protect legal rights and security.</p>
<h2>7. Retention, reset, and your choices</h2><p>Local app progress remains until you reset it or remove the app and its data. The native app’s <strong>Reset local data</strong> control clears saved progress, preferences, migration backups, protection, and scheduled reminders. It does not delete Apple Health records, cancel subscriptions, or remove separate device backups. Manage those with Apple. Removing local data cannot recall a milestone that you already shared.</p><p>We keep support correspondence for as long as needed to handle the request and related follow-up, or meet applicable legal obligations. Purchase providers may retain transaction records under their own retention policies and legal obligations. Contact us to request access, correction, or deletion of information we hold about you, or to ask about applicable privacy rights. We may need to verify a request. We cannot retrieve step history that exists only on your device.</p>
<h2>8. Children and security</h2><p>FeedFare is a general-audience app and does not offer child accounts or a child-directed social service. A parent or guardian should supervise use by children and use Apple’s age, purchase, and permission controls. Contact us if you believe a child has sent personal information to us so we can address it.</p><p>We use the platform’s app storage and permission mechanisms and HTTPS for this website. No storage or transmission method is completely secure. Keep your device and operating system up to date.</p>
<h2>9. Policy updates</h2><p>We will update this page when the app’s practices change and revise the date above. Material changes will be explained here and, when appropriate, in the app or its release information. Where required, we will request consent before a new use of information.</p><p><a href="mailto:nick@nickrae.net">Contact Nick Rae about privacy</a></p>'''

terms='''<p class="legal-date">Updated October 11, 2026 · Effective October 5, 2026</p><div class="callout"><p>These terms cover FeedFare’s walking and screen-time features. Purchases, refunds, and subscriptions also follow the applicable Apple App Store terms. Native FeedFare 2026.9.28 includes the full app without a required subscription. Older installed subscription versions and separate TestFlight builds may have different features or limits.</p></div>
<h2>1. Using FeedFare</h2><p>FeedFare is an independent app developed by Nick Rae. It helps you connect walking with intentional screen time. Use it lawfully and only on devices you are authorized to manage. You do not need a FeedFare account. If you are not legally able to agree to these terms, use the app with a parent or guardian who agrees on your behalf. Apple’s age, account, and purchase requirements also apply.</p>
<h2>2. Permissions and feature availability</h2><p>Step tracking depends on Health and/or Motion access. App protection depends on Screen Time authorization and Apple’s system services. Reminders are optional. Features, limits, and appearance may differ between native releases, older installed versions, and TestFlight builds. Permission changes, system restrictions, device settings, and delayed Health updates can affect operation.</p><p>FeedFare is not an unbreakable lock, a security system, medical advice, or a promise of a particular health or behavior outcome. Choose activity appropriate for your circumstances and keep access to anything essential. Do not use the app as the sole way to supervise another person or enforce a safety-critical restriction.</p>
<h2>3. Purchases and previous subscriptions</h2><p>The App Store shows the current version, price, purchase terms, eligibility, and supported devices for your region. Native FeedFare 2026.9.28 is available on the App Store for supported iPhone and iPad devices. Check Apple’s listing for compatibility and availability in your region. New downloads of the native app use a one-time purchase with the full native app included; there is no in-app paywall, trial, or required subscription in this version. Existing FeedFare owners receive full native access when they install the update on a supported device using the Apple Account that owns the app. This page does not change an existing purchase or subscription.</p><p>FeedFare’s previous subscription plans have been retired and no longer renew. Installing the native app is separate from that change. You can review previous charges and any remaining subscription period in <a href="https://apps.apple.com/account/subscriptions">Apple’s subscription settings</a>. The native app includes full access without an ongoing subscription.</p><p>Apple processes payment and determines eligibility for App Store refunds under its policies and applicable law. <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/118223">Learn how to request a refund from Apple</a>. Nothing here takes away mandatory consumer rights.</p>
<h2>4. Your information</h2><p>Our <a href="https://feedfare.app/privacy-policy.html">privacy policy</a> explains step data, local storage, permissions, legacy purchase processing, support messages, and website hosting. You choose whether to share a milestone through your device’s share sheet. Share only information you are comfortable sending to the selected destination.</p>
<h2>5. Ownership and license</h2><p>FeedFare’s software, branding, and original content belong to Nick Rae or their respective licensors. Your use of the app is subject to Apple’s applicable software license and these terms. Do not copy or redistribute the app or misuse its services except as permitted by the license or applicable law. These terms do not give us a license to publish your private step history.</p>
<h2>6. Availability and limitations</h2><p>We aim to keep FeedFare useful and reliable, but do not guarantee uninterrupted availability, perfect step counts, or protection in every device state. The app is provided as available, subject to warranties and rights that cannot lawfully be excluded. TestFlight software may change or expire. We may update features and will communicate material changes to paid access when required.</p><p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, Nick Rae is not liable for indirect or consequential losses resulting from use of FeedFare, and total liability is limited to the greater of the amount you paid for FeedFare in the preceding 12 months or US $50. These limits do not apply where prohibited by law and do not limit rights that cannot be waived.</p>
<h2>7. Changes and contact</h2><p>We may update these terms to reflect changes to FeedFare or applicable requirements. The updated date will appear here, with notice of material changes where required. California law governs these terms to the extent it does not override mandatory protections where you live. Contact <a href="mailto:nick@nickrae.net">nick@nickrae.net</a> with questions about FeedFare or these terms.</p>'''

support='''<p>This guide covers native FeedFare 2026.9.28. Older installed subscription versions may use different button names or limits. Check the App Store for the latest version supported by your device.</p><nav class="toc" aria-label="Support topics"><a href="#permissions">Permissions</a><a href="#steps">Step updates</a><a href="#screen-time">App protection</a><a href="#billing">Purchases</a><a href="#reset">Reset</a><a href="#contact">Contact</a></nav>
<h2 id="permissions">Connect the features you want</h2><ul><li><strong>Apple Health:</strong> in FeedFare Settings, choose Connect or refresh Health and allow access to step counts. You can review access from Apple Health’s app permissions.</li><li><strong>Motion &amp; Fitness:</strong> use Enable live steps. If permission was denied, review FeedFare under iPhone Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Motion &amp; Fitness, then return and retry.</li><li><strong>Screen Time:</strong> choose Connect Screen Time and complete Apple’s authorization prompt. On the native app, an existing connection shows Manage protected apps instead.</li><li><strong>Reminders:</strong> choose whether to enable the evening check-in. You can change notification permission in iPhone Settings.</li></ul><p>System restrictions can prevent permission changes. If an option is unavailable on a managed device, check with the person who manages it. Do not share your Apple Account password with support.</p>
<h2 id="steps">My steps are not updating</h2><ol><li>Check that Apple Health itself has recent step data and that FeedFare has access to it.</li><li>Open FeedFare and use Refresh steps or Connect or refresh Health. Apple Watch data may need time to sync to your iPhone.</li><li>For live iPhone counting, enable Motion &amp; Fitness and keep your phone with you as you walk. In the native app, Refresh live steps shows progress and a result, a waiting state, or guidance.</li><li>If a connection is already authorized, iOS may not show another permission prompt. Check the status and latest response instead.</li></ol><p>Live Motion updates are a foreground feature. Background Health updates can arrive later; earned totals may not change immediately while FeedFare is closed. Opening the app refreshes available data. The website’s walking example does not read or track your actual steps.</p>
<h2 id="screen-time">My apps are not protected</h2><ol><li>Check that FeedFare has Screen Time authorization. Open Apps or Settings and connect if needed.</li><li>In the native app, use Manage protected apps or Choose protected apps. Pick individual apps, or choose a category to add its current apps. Newly installed apps need to be selected later.</li><li>Save the selection. The native app supports up to 50 selected apps and does not protect websites. It explains mixed selections before saving.</li><li>End an active session before changing the protected selection. A native session unlocks one chosen app while other selected apps remain protected.</li></ol><p>If protection does not return after a session ends, open FeedFare to reconcile the session, check authorization, and contact support with the app version and what happened. Screen Time permissions and system behavior can affect enforcement.</p>
<h2>Goals, streaks, and earned minutes</h2><p>In the native app, the default earning rule is 100 steps for 5 minutes. Change it in Settings. Changes apply to future credits; they do not rewrite the existing balance. Unused balance carries over. Streaks use a separate 1,000-step daily milestone, so changing your daily goal does not change the streak threshold. Features and limits in older installed subscription versions may differ.</p>
<h2 id="billing">Purchases and previous subscriptions</h2><p>Native FeedFare 2026.9.28 is available on the App Store for a one-time download price of US $4.99 in the United States. Check Apple’s listing for your device’s compatibility and regional price. The full native app is included. This version has no in-app PRO purchase, trial, or required subscription.</p><p>If you already own FeedFare, install the native update through the App Store using the Apple Account that owns the app. Full native access is included on supported devices; you do not need an ongoing FeedFare subscription for this version.</p><p>FeedFare’s previous subscription plans have been retired and no longer renew. Installing the native app is separate from that change. You can review previous charges and any remaining subscription period under Settings → your name → Subscriptions. The native app includes full access without an ongoing subscription.</p><ul><li><a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/118428">Review your previous subscription with Apple</a>.</li><li><a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/118223">Request a refund from Apple</a>. Eligibility depends on Apple’s policies and applicable law.</li><li>If you are still using an older subscription version and access is missing, use that version’s Restore Purchases control with the Apple Account that made the purchase.</li></ul>
<h2 id="reset">Resetting local data</h2><p>In the native app, Settings → Reset local data removes saved progress, balance, preferences, migration backups, app protection, and scheduled reminders on that device. This cannot be undone within the app. It does not delete Apple Health data, manage device backups, or cancel a subscription. Review what you need to keep before confirming a reset.</p>
<h2 id="contact">Still need a hand?</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:nick@nickrae.net?subject=FeedFare%20support">nick@nickrae.net</a> with your FeedFare version/build, iOS version, what you tapped, and what you expected to happen. The native app shows its build in Settings → About FeedFare. Please leave out private Health records, passwords, payment details, and Screen Time tokens. A screenshot with personal information removed can help.</p>'''

for path,title,desc,content in [('privacy-policy.html','Privacy Policy','How FeedFare handles step counts, Screen Time selections, purchases, local data, and website requests.',privacy),('terms.html','Terms of Use','FeedFare terms for walking features, app protection, one-time downloads, and previous subscriptions.',terms),('support.html','A little help, when you need it.','Help with FeedFare permissions, step updates, Screen Time, subscriptions, and local data.',support)]:
    body=f'<main id="main" class="wrap document"><div class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">FeedFare · {("Support" if path=="support.html" else "Clear, useful information")}</p><h1>{title}</h1></div>{content}</main>'
    (ROOT/path).write_text(page(f'{title} — FeedFare',desc,path,body))

press='''<main id="main" class="wrap document press-document"><div class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">For writers, reviewers and creators</p><h1>FeedFare press kit</h1><p class="press-tagline">Walk first. Scroll later.</p></div><p>FeedFare turns walking into earned time for apps you choose. Connect your steps, choose apps to protect, and spend earned minutes on a timed session for one app. You can adjust the walking rule, and unused minutes carry over.</p><p>Built by independent developer Nick Rae, FeedFare is a native SwiftUI app for a more intentional pause before your next scroll.</p><div class="callout"><p><strong>Full app. One purchase.</strong> US $4.99 once, with no required subscription, in-app paywall or FeedFare account. Apple shows regional prices, compatibility and purchase eligibility.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://apps.apple.com/app/id6758923557?ppid=fc80f820-a690-452a-95d4-76c93fce92d7">View FeedFare on the App Store <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><nav class="toc" aria-label="Press kit topics"><a href="#facts">Quick facts</a><a href="#assets">Images</a><a href="#videos">Demonstrations</a><a href="#press-contact">Contact</a></nav>
<h2 id="facts">Quick facts</h2><table><tbody><tr><th scope="row">App</th><td>FeedFare: Earn Screen Time</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Developer</th><td>Nick Rae / Nicholas Rae</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Public version</th><td>2026.9.28</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Devices</th><td>iPhone and iPad; iOS or iPadOS 17 or later</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Category</th><td>Health &amp; Fitness</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Language</th><td>English</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Walking rule</th><td>Default: 100 steps earns 5 minutes. Adjustable in Settings.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Timed access</th><td>One selected app per session; other selected apps stay protected.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Selection limits</th><td>Up to 50 selected apps. Website blocking is not included.</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="press-date">Public offer checked October 11, 2026. Check Apple’s listing for the latest version and your regional price.</p>
<h2>Permissions and privacy</h2><p>Health or Motion &amp; Fitness access supplies steps. Screen Time authorization enables app protection. Reminders are optional. Apple Watch steps can be read after they sync to Health on the iPhone; updates can be delayed.</p><p>Progress and app selections are stored locally in the native app. The native release has no advertising or third-party analytics SDK and does not require a FeedFare account. Apple’s device backup and diagnostic settings still apply. <a href="privacy-policy.html">Read the privacy policy</a> and <a href="support.html#permissions">permission guide</a>.</p><p>FeedFare supports a person’s own app choices. It is not a remote parental-control system or a guarantee of uninterrupted protection. Permission changes and system behavior can affect enforcement. <a href="support.html#screen-time">See protection help and limitations</a>.</p>
<h2 id="assets">Icon and app images</h2><div class="press-icon"><img src="assets/app-icon-128.webp?v=build29" width="128" height="128" alt="FeedFare’s blue footprint app icon." loading="lazy"><div><h3>Approved app icon</h3><p><a href="app-icon.png?v=build29" download="FeedFare-icon.png">Download 1024 × 1024 PNG</a></p></div></div><p>The following images show actual native FeedFare 2026.9.28 screens captured in a simulator with example data. They do not show a customer’s progress or demonstrate physical-device step sensing or enforcement. Keep that context with reproduced images.</p><div class="press-assets">'''+''.join(f'<figure><a href="assets/{name}-native-800.webp" download="FeedFare-{name}-simulator-example.webp">'+image(name,f'Native FeedFare {label} screen captured in a simulator with example data.')+f'</a><figcaption><strong>{label}</strong><a href="assets/{name}-native-800.webp" download="FeedFare-{name}-simulator-example.webp">Download WebP</a><span>Simulator · example data</span></figcaption></figure>' for name,label in [('dashboard','Dashboard'),('activity','Activity'),('stats','Stats')])+'''</div>
<h2 id="videos">Published demonstrations</h2><div class="press-video"><h3>56-second modeled walkthrough</h3><p>A temporary demonstration build illustrates the earning calculation and a five-minute session, with the wait shortened in the edit. Its Demo App controls are not shipping app controls.</p><p><strong>Simulator demonstration. Steps and protection are simulated.</strong> This does not show a physical walk, Health updates, an external app unlocking or iOS Screen Time enforcement.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EQfLgETl0m0">Watch the modeled walkthrough <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="press-video"><h3>24-second walking-rule preview</h3><p>Actual simulator UI shows the walking rule changing from 100 to 150 steps and from 5 to 6 minutes. Progress is example data, and step connections and protection are off in this recording. It is an interface preview.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.youtube.com/shorts/QO57QRxTYs0">Watch the Settings preview <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><p>Keep the simulator and example-data disclosures intact when sharing either video. Reviewers should test the public app on their own supported device.</p>
<h2 id="press-contact">Contact Nick</h2><p>For editorial questions or a walkthrough of the app, contact <a href="mailto:nick@nickrae.net?subject=FeedFare%20press">nick@nickrae.net</a>. Candid setup feedback is welcome.</p><p><a href="https://nickrae.net">About Nick Rae</a> · <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@FeedFareApp">YouTube @FeedFareApp</a> · <a href="https://x.com/FeedFareApp">X @FeedFareApp</a></p><p><a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/id6758923557?ppid=fc80f820-a690-452a-95d4-76c93fce92d7">App Store</a> · <a href="support.html">Setup and support</a> · <a href="privacy-policy.html">Privacy policy</a></p></main>'''
(ROOT/'press.html').write_text(page('FeedFare press kit — Walk first. Scroll later.','Current FeedFare facts, approved icon and native app images, labeled simulator demonstrations, and contact details for writers and creators.','press.html',press))

(ROOT/'404.html').write_text(page('Page not found — FeedFare','Find your way back to FeedFare.','404.html','<main id="main" class="wrap not-found"><p class="eyebrow">404 · A small detour</p><h1>Let’s get you<br>back on your path.</h1><p>That page is not here. Your next step is.</p><a class="button" href="https://feedfare.app/">Back to FeedFare <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></main>',noindex=True).replace('href="assets/','href="https://feedfare.app/assets/').replace('src="assets/','src="https://feedfare.app/assets/'))
